.TH ALLINONEPDF 1 "" "AllInOne PDF" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
allinonepdf \- convert, read, style and lay out PDFs, all offline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B allinonepdf
[\fIoption\fR] [\fIfile\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
AllInOne PDF turns files into PDFs and PDFs into files (Markdown, HTML, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, RTF, EPUB, text,
images and more), reads them in a reflowable view, styles PDFs with themes and lays out publications in the Creator.
Without an option the application window opens.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-paths
Print where settings, themes, history and output go, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-check\-assets " [\fIfile\fR]"
Check that the window can load every file it needs, then exit. Writes the report to \fIfile\fR, or to the console.
The exit code is 1 if anything is missing.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show the help, then exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/AllInOnePdf
Settings, themes, history, publications, the browser cache and crash logs. Delete it (with the app closed) to start
fresh.
.TP
.I AllInOne PDF
Default folder for converted files, in the Documents folder (or the home folder when there is none).
.TP
.I /opt/allinonepdf
The program and its bundled .NET runtime.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ALLINONEPDF_DATA_DIR
Use this folder for data instead of ~/.config/AllInOnePdf.
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/rndadhdman/AllInOnePDF/issues
